The default-off `--additional-axioms` option also exposes closed identities for concrete native integer literal arguments of function calls. It retains the original arguments and checks, deduplicates numerals per translated module, and emits them in numerical order. The unchanged bitvector shift-by-zero example now passes on pinned Z3 4.12.1 and 5.1.0 at the existing regression cap in both resolver modes. Symbolic, real and boxed arguments, pruning and solver settings are unchanged.
